504	     * minimum charge (in its currency), or else the workspace's minimum charge, converted from US dollars at the
505	     * pricing date's rate (see {@link #pricingDate}) and rounded down to the step. Nothing when no minimum is set (or the client's is 0), for a
506	     * credit note, or for an invoice with no lines; on an adjustment credit note, the part it keeps back (see {@link #keepMinimum}),
507	     * which does not come off and is taxed at the standard rate on its own.
508	     */
509	    public BigDecimal minimumCharge() {
510	        if (isKeepingMinimum()) {
511	            return getMinimumKept();
512	        }
513	        if (isCreditNote() || isAdjustment() || lines.isEmpty()) {
514	            return zero();
515	        }
516	        BigDecimal minimum = minimum();
517	        return minimum == null ? zero() : minimum.subtract(discounted().add(surcharge())).max(zero());
